      "created_at": "2017-12-03T13:15:43Z",
      "updated_at": "2017-12-03T13:15:43Z",
      "body": "hi @joonasp sorry for the late response, I had a number of issues that past my tracking and I am currently coming back to them. \r\n\r\nWe are waiting for a detailed assessment of the changes we need to have to comply with GDPR, if you have a list that is more detailed than what you have included as bullet-point is will certainly help.\r\n\r\nFor Decidim it is difficult to asses what is \"personal info\" since we only store hashing of minimal personal information, and what I got as a result of asking some experts is that hashes don't constitute personal information (but I would like a second opinion on this). \r\n\r\nAs @mrcasals says there are some issues tagged with `privacy` but these are more focused on ethical and political aspects than complying directly with the GDPR directive. \r\n\r\nAt Barcelona City Council we are undergoing a widespread effort to comply with GDPR and I am still waiting for a specific set of recommendations. Lets turn back to this issue as soon as I get feedback.",
